					3. Open Barrier vs. Closed Distance Toll Collection Systems
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm text-mapa-ink/80 leading-relaxed mb-4">
					Philippine highways use two distinct engineering models for fare collection:
				</p>
				<ul class="space-y-3 text-xs text-mapa-ink/80 list-disc pl-5 leading-relaxed">
					<li>
						<strong>Open Barrier System:</strong> Motorists pay a fixed, flat toll fee upon passing a physical barrier plaza, regardless of the distance traveled within that segment. Examples include NLEX Balintawak (₱74), Skyway Buendia entry (₱164), NAIAX (₱45), and CCLEX (₱90).
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Closed Distance-Based System:</strong> Motorists tap in at their entry interchange (where an electronic timestamp and entry tag are logged) and tap out at their exit interchange. The toll fee is computed precisely per kilometer based on the distance between the two interchanges. Examples include NLEX north of Bocaue, SLEX south of Alabang, SCTEX, TPLEX, and CALAX.
